      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off the side, plan and front views (tools/trace/b736/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. Plain wing tips, as the sheet draws them (few 737-600s carry winglets). The drawing has no cabin windows: they're placed at the 737's frame pitch on the overwing exit, at the 737-800's height. The eyebrow windows are left out, as on the 737-700 and -800. The side view draws the engine's inlet lip 9.08 m from the nose where the sheet prints 8.84 m (its plan view draws it at 9.38 m): the nacelle is moved 0.24 m forward to the printed figure (build.py, as for any inlet more than 1.5% off). This sheet also draws the fin about 0.3 m further aft on the tail cone than the 737-700W's sheet does; kept as drawn."
    }
